---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfessionalService',
  name: 'Vemor',
  description: 'AI automation and managed operations for small businesses. Founded by a 14-year industry operator. Bilingual, English and Spanish.',
  url: 'https://vemor.ai',
  priceRange: '$$',
  areaServed: ['San Diego', 'Southern California', 'United States', 'Mexico'],
};
---
<Base
  title="Vemor | AI Automation & AI Voice Agents for Small Business, San Diego"
  description="AI automation and a bilingual AI voice agent for small business in San Diego. Phones answered, books reconciled, busywork gone. Built and run by operators, not just engineers."
  schema={schema}
  path="/"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="hero-tagline">AI Automation &amp; Managed Operations</span>
    <h1>AI automation built by people <span class="gold">who've done your job.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Vemor was founded on 14 years of running small businesses, managing insurance
      operations, and living the busywork we now automate. We build the systems that
      kill it, and we run them for you. In English y en español.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Tell us what's eating your time</a>
      <a href="/voice" class="btn-secondary">Hear the AI receptionist</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-proof">
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">14+</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Years inside small business operations</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">1,000+</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Businesses visited in the field</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">EN / ES</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Bilingual, natively. Other languages too.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <span class="proof-value">24/7</span>
        <span class="proof-label">Systems that run while you sleep</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STORY (CSC land-and-expand) -->
  <div class="section-full soft" id="results">
    <div class="inner">
      <span class="label">Real Work, Real Client</span>
      <h2 class="title">It started with one report. It became four systems.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        A four-location smog inspection operation in San Diego's South Bay. This is how
        Vemor engagements actually go: one problem solved, then the next one.
      </p>
      <div class="story-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="story-stats">
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">30+ hrs/wk</div>
              <div class="stat-label">of manual reconciliation, eliminated</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">Same day</div>
              <div class="stat-label">payment errors caught, not weeks later</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">4 systems</div>
              <div class="stat-label">live: reporting, RFID tracking, AI phones, security</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
              <div class="stat-value">Month 1</div>
              <div class="stat-label">"The system paid for itself"</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="story-content">
          <h4>Where it started</h4>
          <p>
            Reconciling sales across four stations was a full-time job. Five days a
            week of comparing printouts, hunting voided invoices, checking discounts,
            and finding payment errors. And mistakes still slipped through for weeks.
          </p>
          <h4>What Vemor built</h4>
          <p>
            An automated pipeline that reads their existing point-of-sale database
            every night, reconciles everything, flags exceptions, and emails a clean
            report before opening. What used to be a full-time job is now about an
            hour a day of reviewing reports that are already done.
          </p>
          <h4>What happened next</h4>
          <p>
            Trust earned, the next problem came up: rental equipment going missing.
            Vemor built RFID tracking across all four locations. Then a bilingual AI
            agent for the phones. Then security management. One relationship, four
            systems, all running today as a managed service.
          </p>
          <div class="pull-quote">"The system paid for itself in the first month."</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WHAT WE DO -->
  <section id="services">
    <span class="label">What We Do</span>
    <h2 class="title">Ways to work with Vemor.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Start with your phones, fix one workflow, hand off your operations, or get the settlement data your case needs. Every client is different, so every engagement is different. What's the same: you get the finished result, not a tool you have to figure out.</p>
    <div class="cards-3" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-badge">Start Here</span>
        <h3>Vemor Voice</h3>
        <p class="tagline">Your phones answered. 24/7.</p>
        <p>
          An AI receptionist that answers every call, books appointments, handles
          FAQs, and hands off to a human when it matters. English and Spanish
          mid-call, natively. Italian, French, and most major languages available.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Live in days, not months</li>
          <li>Books straight into your calendar</li>
          <li>Weekly report of every call and booking</li>
          <li>Flat monthly rate, no per-minute games</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/voice" class="card-cta">Hear it live →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-badge">One Problem, Solved</span>
        <h3>Custom Builds</h3>
        <p class="tagline">One workflow, fixed scope.</p>
        <p>
          A single system, built around one problem that hurts: a reconciliation
          report, a customer database, a document pipeline, automated outreach.
          Clear scope, clear price, built on the tools you already use.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Starts with a paid operations audit</li>
          <li>You keep the system and the roadmap</li>
          <li>Managed by Vemor, or handed over</li>
          <li>Most builds grow into ongoing work</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/builds" class="card-cta">How it works →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card featured">
        <span class="card-badge">The Core Service</span>
        <h3>Managed AI Operations</h3>
        <p class="tagline">Your operations, handled end to end.</p>
        <p>
          Vemor finds the busywork eating your week, builds the automation that
          kills it, and then runs it. You get a builder and an operator on your
          team, not a consultant with a slide deck.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Audit, architect, build, operate, expand</li>
          <li>Ongoing monitoring and weekly reporting</li>
          <li>One accountable partner, not a platform</li>
          <li>Nothing locks you in. Ever.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/operations" class="card-cta">The full service →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-badge">For Law Firms</span>
        <h3>Vemor Comps</h3>
        <p class="tagline">PAGA settlement data. Verified.</p>
        <p>
          Verified PAGA settlement comparables for California attorneys. Every figure
          matched verbatim to the filed document, delivered with the source filings
          attached. Reports, working Excel, and benchmark statistics. Updated daily.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>20,000+ PAGA matters tracked</li>
          <li>Every figure verified against source text</li>
          <li>Source documents ship with the report</li>
          <li>24-48 hour turnaround for firms in the corpus</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/comps" class="card-cta">Learn more →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
  <div class="section-full soft">
    <div class="inner">
      <span class="label">The Process</span>
      <h2 class="title">Five steps. No mystery.</h2>
      <p class="sub">The same process behind every system Vemor runs today.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">1</div>
          <h3>Audit</h3>
          <p>We map where your time actually goes and find the automation worth doing first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">2</div>
          <h3>Architect</h3>
          <p>We design the system around your existing tools. Build what's needed, buy what's smarter, skip the rest.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">3</div>
          <h3>Build</h3>
          <p>Vemor builds it: automations, AI agents, databases, integrations, hardware if the job calls for it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">4</div>
          <h3>Operate</h3>
          <p>We run it. Monitoring, maintenance, reports. You don't need an IT department.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">5</div>
          <h3>Expand</h3>
          <p>When the next thing hurts, we automate that too. Trust first, always.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WHY TRUST -->
  <section>
    <span class="label">Why Owners Trust Vemor</span>
    <h2 class="title">If Vemor disappeared tomorrow, your business wouldn't notice.</h2>
    <p class="sub">That's not modesty. That's the design principle behind everything we build.</p>
    <div class="cards-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Built on what you have</h3>
        <p>
          Every Vemor system sits on top of your existing tools. Your point-of-sale
          stays your point-of-sale. Your calendar stays your calendar. Your data
          stays yours. No platform migrations, no rip-and-replace, no new software
          your team has to learn.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Leave whenever you want</h3>
        <p>
          Forward your phone line to the AI agent; unforward it and you're back
          where you started. No long contracts, no data held hostage, no system
          only we can operate. Vemor keeps clients by being useful, not by locking
          the door.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Operators, not just engineers</h3>
        <p>
          Vemor learned these problems by living them: years running shop
          operations, writing estimates, walking into a thousand businesses in the
          field. And when your industry is new to us, the first thing we do is get
          inside your workflow, because the busywork patterns are the same
          everywhere.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NORTH STAR -->
  <div class="section-full soft north-star">
    <p class="north-star-text">"Vemor exists because <em>life's too short</em> to spend it on busywork."</p>
  </div>

  <!-- FINAL CTA -->
  <section style="text-align:center;">
    <h2 class="title">Ready to get your time back?</h2>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;">
      Twenty minutes, no pitch deck. Tell us what's eating your week and you'll get
      a straight answer on whether it's worth automating.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas" style="justify-content:center;">
      <a href="https://Vemor.as.me/" class="btn-primary">Book a Call</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary">Send a Message</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
